# Guarantee /opt exists (root-writable, 0755) on the installed Sysible Workstation.
#
# base-files ships /opt, but an EMPTY directory can be dropped when the live
# filesystem is squashed and copied to the target by the live installer —
# leaving the controller and vendor tools (which install under /opt/sysible)
# with nowhere to go, and `/opt` "missing" on first boot. This placeholder file
# forces /opt into the chroot -> squashfs -> installed system so it is always
# present. Safe to leave in place.
